  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Reduction of and Improved Operational Response to Gender-Based Violence through Camp Management and Site Planning Phase IX</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2015, IOM has been implementing a global project on reducing gender-based violence (GBV) through enhanced institutional risk mitigation efforts under the Safe from the Start Initiative (SftS) supported by the US Bureau of Population, Refugees and Migration (PRM). IOM&apos;s Global SftS project entitled &quot;Promoting the Reduction of and Improved Operational Response to Gender-Based Violence through Camp Management and Site Planning,&quot; is now entering its ninth year. In Phase IX, IOM continues to pursue key milestones set against commitments made by IOM under the 2021-2025 Roadmap of the Global Call to Action on Protection against GBV in Emergencies including: to strengthen risk mitigation and response capacities in key technical areas where IOM brings a strategic added-value to collective efforts on GBV - including Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), Shelter and Settlements, and Health; to pursue the institutionalization and operationalization of the GBV in Crises (GBViC) Framework to foster more coherent and holistic responses of IOM to address GBV in crisis; and to continue supporting inter-agency initiatives from the Inter-Agency Standing Committee (IASC) and UN-wide system on collective Protection against Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (PSEA).</narrative>
  </description>
